name issue_437_default_flip_very_low_capacity
describe very_low_capacity with the defaults: libwebrtc's pre-render queue and keyframe padding flush are on
# 80 seeds in compare-webrtc (#739): render fps is in band there (yardstick #798).
compare_seeds 80
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=100kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
# Issue #437: libwebrtc renders through IncomingVideoStream / VideoRenderFrames by
# default (enable_prerenderer_smoothing = true, call/video_receive_stream.h:291 at
# M157; video/video_receive_stream2.cc:400-403), and a keyframe's pacer flush also
# clears the padding queued on the RTX SSRC (modules/pacing/pacing_controller.cc:227-231).
# This scenario sets neither switch, so it runs the library's defaults. Before the
# flip (both off) seed 1 rendered at 12.55 fps; seeds 1-5 off -> on:
# 12.55/13.57/12.68/10.05/12.32 -> 10.75/11.05/11.25/5.25/11.10.
# Seeds 1-10 render fps 11.07 -> 9.66 against libwebrtc's 8.30 (band +-1.25), longest
# freeze 3864 -> 4138 ms against 4431 (band +-465): in band.
# Target (issue #437): libwebrtc's rendered frames on this link (8.3 fps, 10 seeds).
# Issue #860 (guard rail during a port, needs-human): one datagram per RTCP send call moves seed 1
# to 12.28 (seeds 1-10 mean 9.41 -> 9.72; libwebrtc 8.30, worst seed 9.88). The first difference
# from libwebrtc's trace on this link is at 630 ms, before and after #860 (RTX sequence numbers).
expect video.render_fps < 12.3
expect audio.concealed_pct < 20
expect net.loss_pct < 45
expect video.keyframe_requests < 300
